## Start here

This Android upload package contains 449 separately viewable, full-dimension images covering 516 labeled source records. It includes all 70 matched current viewpoints as 140 separate Claudia/candidate files. Every approved image keeps the original bytes. Gameplay review JPEGs retain the full source pixel grid. FILE_INDEX.csv identifies pixel-identical historical aliases and the compression applied per file.

The five folders are Screen_04, Screen_05, Screen_06, Screen_07 and Screen_08. Each number refers to a playable stage in the existing Rainbow Android game. Benny is the pink swimmer in the purple-and-white beanie.

For an independent review, inspect the artwork, retained ride and candidate at the same stage position. Write down what you see before checking the supplied observations.

1. In the image package, open the full-screen SCREEN##_APPROVED.jpg. All five are exact copies of the original approved files. Screen 05 also has a separate original water-detail reference.

2. In Current/, compare SCREEN##_CLAUDIA_OPENING and SCREEN##_CODEX_CANDIDATE_OPENING. Continue with the same FORWARD, HARD_LEFT, HARD_RIGHT, MIDDLE, DEEP, stage-specific feature, FINAL_APPROACH and STAGE_TRANSITION filenames. The FILE_INDEX.csv identifies every source and any identical shared picture.

3. In the video package, open SCREEN##_CLAUDIA_RETAINED_ENTRANCE_TO_EXIT.mp4 and SCREEN##_CODEX_CANDIDATE_ENTRANCE_TO_EXIT.mp4 directly inside the matching screen folder. These are the ten primary clips. Compare the same timestamp in each.

4. On Android, attach the two master ZIPs in the same conversation when your app accepts them. If the app cannot open a ZIP, extract one small stage batch in your Files app and attach its original artwork and matched screenshots. The download page also offers the individual MP4s. If video playback is unavailable in chat, the named stills and frame logs show the important positions.

