## Camera, gameplay and measurements

The photographed opening is the single exact design viewpoint for each stage. Native current stills are 864 × 1536 pixels, DPR 1, with matched camera transform, position, steering and shader clock. Opening, entrance and the first frame of the ride are different positions. CAMERA_POSES.csv gives the actual values.

The primary clips replay the retained real Three.js renderer using the saved fixed-step ride. The CSS viewport remains 324 × 576, the drawing buffer is 648 × 1152, and the stream is H.264 at 12 fps. There are five 1/60-second game steps per recorded frame. Every frame was checked against its original ride for course position, lateral movement, steering, camera, shader clock, hearts and score. The original 324 × 576 recordings are also packaged. Higher physical pixel density changes antialiasing and texture sampling. The GitHub evidence commits identify the saved original rides and images. The high-detail MP4s are fresh exports from those revisions for these packages. Their SHA-256 values are in HD_REPLAY_VERIFICATION.json. That file’s correlation statistic compares two recordings of the same game. OPENING_MEASUREMENTS.json contains the comparison to your original artwork. The higher-detail exports have no separate GitHub commit.

RGB agreement counts the whole-frame fraction with mean absolute RGB error at most 20 on a 0–255 scale. Pixelmatch 7.1.0 uses threshold 0.1 with antialias mismatches excluded. The reports measure the original source pixels, including Benny and the HUD. Full-size review JPEGs can change individual channel values. For pixel-level work use the standalone native-image ZIP parts.

Use visual judgment for unpictured moving viewpoints. The reference establishes materials, shapes and composition at its photographed viewpoint. The camera beyond that viewpoint and hidden surfaces require interpretation. An exact reference percentage for the unseen route is unavailable.

Both retained and candidate builds passed eight gameplay assertions, collected 91 coins, and advanced the full-game score from 1,330 to 2,240. All ten primary stage rides retained five hearts, and all five saved across-transition images matched their baseline exactly. Screen 04’s ordinary full-game coin run lost one heart in both builds. A separate full-game safe route collected 91 and finished at 2,240 with five hearts in each. Screen 08’s separate full-steer collision stills cost one heart in both versions.

